[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked known, one issue and one fix. Read report by report, it holds
three different problems. Each now has its own ticket.

<Callout>
Not known. Only the first problem has a fix queued.
</Callout>

## What is in it

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table groups reports by the tenant's locale and booking form, not by intake's browser guess.
The count is of unique report ids: the export repeats some reports. The table has no cause for the one-day reports, so it counts them under `parser` (379). Without them the parser has 374.

## The three problems

1. **Parser reads dates month first.** Day-first tenants get day and month swapped. This is what #4471 was named after. Ticket: [issue 1](https://github.com/kyrstke/mega-dev-sandbox/issues/1), 374 reports.
2. **booking-v3 hint says MM/DD/YYYY.** People at day-first tenants type what the hint says. The fix is the hint, not the parser. Ticket: [issue 2](https://github.com/kyrstke/mega-dev-sandbox/issues/2), 33 reports.
3. **Dates off by exactly one day.** Not a month swap; likely a timezone problem. The table counts these under the parser, and the desk notes mark them. Ticket: [issue 3](https://github.com/kyrstke/mega-dev-sandbox/issues/3), 5 reports (inside the table's 379).

## Lessons

- Merging by subject line hid two bugs inside the biggest ticket. Count by cause, not by wording.
- Intake's tag is a guess. The tenant tells you the cause.

